{"abstract":"We report the discovery of TOI-4641b, a warm Jupiter transiting a rapidly rotating F-type star with a stellar effective temperature of 6560 K. The planet has a radius of 0.73 RJup, a mass smaller than 3.87 MJup(3σ), and a period of 22.09 d. It is orbiting a bright star (V=7.5 mag) on a circular orbit with a radius and mass of 1.73 R⊙ and 1.41 M⊙. Follow-up ground-based photometry was obtained using the Tierras Observatory. Two transits were also observed with the Tillinghast Reflector Echelle Spectrograph, revealing the star to have a low projected spin-orbit angle (λ=1.41+0.76/-0.76). Such obliquity measurements for stars with warm Jupiters are relatively few, and may shed light on the formation of warm Jupiters. Among the known planets orbiting hot and rapidly rotating stars, TOI-4641b is one of the longest period planets to be thoroughly characterized. Unlike hot Jupiters around hot stars which are more often misaligned, the warm Jupiter TOI-4641b is found in a well-aligned orbit. Future exploration of this parameter space can add one more dimension to the star–planet orbital obliquity distribution that has been well sampled for hot Jupiters.","author_count":28,"contributors":["Bieryla, Allyson","Zhou, George","García-Mejía, Juliana","Fairnington, Tyler R.","Latham, David W.","Carter, Brad","Dong, Jiayin","Huang, Chelsea X.","Murphy, Simon J.","Shporer, Avi","Collins, Karen A.","Quinn, Samuel N.","Everett, Mark E.","Buchhave, Lars A.","Tronsgaard, René","Charbonneau, David","Johnson, Marshall C.","Esquerdo, Gilbert A.","Calkins, Michael","Berlind, Perry","Jenkins, Jon M.","Ricker, George R.","Seager, Sara","Winn, Joshua N.","Barclay, Thomas","Mireles, Ismael","Paegert, Martin","Twicken, Joseph D."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718529"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Bieryla, Allyson"],"country":["Australia","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard-Smithsonian Center for Astrophysics","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","NASA Ames Research Center","NASA Goddard Space Flight Center","NSF’s National Optical-Infrared Astronomy Research Laboratory","Ohio State University","Princeton University","SETI Institute","Simons Foundation","University of New Mexico","University of Southern Queensland"],"keyword":["Exoplanets","Techniques photometric","Techniques radial velocities","Techniques spectroscopic"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toi 000000004641b an aligned warm jupiter orbiting a bright v 000000000007 000000000005 rapidly rotating f star","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/stad3785","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718529","identifier":[{"id":"85183375759","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-48f064bd-1e07-4df4-b728-5f3ac7947f45"],"keyword":["Exoplanets","Methods: observãtional","Techniques: photometric","Techniques: radial velocities","Techniques: spectroscopic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-72523039A0150058FEDC11C87D41BA1A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/stad3785","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/351178725/stad3785.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"harvard smithsonian center for astrophysics","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard-Smithsonian Center for Astrophysics","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"university of southern queensland","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Southern Queensland","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"simons foundation","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Simons Foundation","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"nsf s national optical infrared astronomy research laboratory","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"NSF’s National Optical-Infrared Astronomy Research Laboratory","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology, Astrophysics and Atmospheric Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"ohio state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Ohio State University","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"us","key":"nasa ames research center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"NASA Ames Research Center","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"us","key":"princeton university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Princeton University","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"us","key":"nasa goddard space flight center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"NASA Goddard Space Flight Center","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"us","key":"university of new mexico","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of New Mexico","used":1},{"affno":"12","country":"us","key":"seti institute","loc":["United States","