{"abstract":"We have detected solar-like oscillations in the mid-K-dwarf ϵ Indi A, making it the coolest dwarf to have measured oscillations. The star is noteworthy for harboring a pair of brown dwarf companions and a Jupiter-type planet. We observed ϵ Indi A during two radial velocity campaigns, using the high-resolution spectrographs HARPS (2011) and UVES (2021). Weighting the time series, we computed the power spectra and established the detection of solar-like oscillations with a power excess located at 5265 ± 110 μHz—the highest frequency solar-like oscillations so far measured in any star. The measurement of the center of the power excess allows us to compute a stellar mass of 0.782 ± 0.023 M ⊙ based on scaling relations and a known radius from interferometry. We also determine the amplitude of the peak power and note that there is a slight difference between the two observing campaigns, indicating a varying activity level. Overall, this work confirms that low-amplitude solar-like oscillations can be detected in mid-K-type stars in radial velocity measurements obtained with high-precision spectrographs.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Lundkvist, M.","Kjeldsen, Hans","Bedding, Timothy R.","McCaughrean, Mark J.","Butler, R. Paul","Slumstrup, Ditte","Campante, Tiago L.","Aerts, Conny","Arentoft, T.","Bruntt, H.","Cardoso, Cátia V.","Carrier, Fabien","Close, Laird M.","da Silva, João Gomes","Kallinger, Thomas","King, Robert R.","Li, Yaguang","Murphy, Simon J.","Mosumgaard, Jakob Rørsted","Stello, Dennis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-736625"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Lundkvist, M."],"country":["Australia","Austria","Belgium","Chile","Germany","Netherlands","Portugal","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Science","European Southern Observatory","European Space Research and Technology Centre (ESTEC)","KU Leuven","Universidad Diego Portales","University of Arizona","University of Exeter","University of Hawaii at Manoa","University of New South Wales","University of Porto","University of Southern Queensland","University of Sydney","University of Vienna"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low amplitude solar like oscillations in the k000000000005 v star ϵ indi a","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4357/ad25f2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-736625","identifier":[{"id":"85188911190","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-05845ac8-7cac-4924-bfac-54365edff662"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-32DB6C48E55437CB8468C3871E3861CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4357/ad25f2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"university of sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Sydney","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"european space research and technology centre","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"European Space Research and Technology Centre (ESTEC)","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"carnegie science","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Carnegie Science","used":1},{