{"abstract":"Explainable AI (XAI) is pivotal for understanding complex ’black-box’ models, particularly in text analysis, where transparency is essential yet challenging. This paper introduces SIDU-TXT, an adaptation of the ’Similarity Difference and Uniqueness’ (SIDU) method, originally applied in image classification, to textual data. SIDU-TXT generates word-level heatmaps using feature activation maps, highlighting contextually important textual elements for model predictions. Given the absence of a unified standard for assessing XAI methods, to evaluate SIDU-TXT, we implement a comprehensive three-tiered evaluation framework – Functionally-Grounded, Human-Grounded, and Application-Grounded – across varied experimental setups. Our findings show SIDU-TXT’s effectiveness in sentiment analysis, outperforming benchmarks like Grad-CAM and LIME in both Functionally and Human-Grounded assessments. In a legal domain application involving complex asylum decision-making, SIDU-TXT displays competitive but not conclusive results, underscoring the nuanced expectations of domain experts. This work advances the field by offering a methodical holistic approach to XAI evaluation in NLP, urging further research to bridge the existing gap in expert expectations and refine interpretability methods for intricate applications. The study underscores the critical role of extensive evaluations in fostering AI technologies that are not only technically faithful to the model but also comprehensible and trustworthy for end-users.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jahromi, Mohammad Naser Sabet","Muddamsetty, Satya Mahesh","Stage Jarlner, Asta Sofie","Høgenhaug, Anna Murphy","Gammeltoft-Hansen, Thomas","Moeslund, Thomas B."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-767011"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jahromi, Mohammad Naser Sabet"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sidu txt an xai algorithm for nlp with a holistic assessment approach","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nlp.2024.100078","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-767011","ids":["aau-c5c122ff-570b-48ab-b588-3758014004f7","ku-77070121-1ac9-48e2-81d6-4acacf1e81f6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-356D7673785DF8173C7AF225DDC6EBDB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/770409595/1-s2.0-S2949719124000268-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nlp.2024.100078","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Centre for AI Ethics, Law and Policy","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Visual Analysis and Perception"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":