2.0-85159241898"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-89cc9675-675c-4108-a8ec-0ecd355eb155"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A nutritional biomarker score of the Mediterranean diet and incident type 2 diabetes : Integrated analysis of data from the MedLey randomised controlled trial and the EPIC-InterAct case-cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-678609","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Catadromous European eel (Anguilla anguilla) are a critically endangered fish species due in part to in-river anthropogenic barriers (e.g., pumping stations, weirs, hydropower facilities). European legislation stipulates that safe downstream passage must be provided at hazardous intakes. Where present, gravity sluices have the potential to act as safe and low-cost downstream passage for seaward migrating silver eels at pumping station, but operational changes are required. This study used catchment-wide and fine-scale acoustic telemetry to investigate if operational changes (OC) at a pumping station (PS) with a co-located gravity sluice (GS) facilitated safe downstream passage for silver European eels. Specifically, night-time pump operations were ceased, river levels prior to sluicing were elevated and the GS was opened during key eel migration windows, i.e., at night during the new moon phase in autumn. No tagged eels passed through any pumps and the majority (2018 = 87.5%, 2020 = 88.9%) that approached the PS during OC passed downstream through the GS. Most eels approached during the first period of night sluicing after release (2018 = 73.9% and 2020 = 76.5%) and passed downstream during the first sluice event they experienced at the PS (2018 = 66.7% and 2020 = 75.0%). During the final approach prior to passage, very few retreats back upstream occurred at a median (IQR) distance of 34 (7.25) m from the GS and were predominantly a short distance (1–8 m). Overall, OC at a PS with a GS are considered a win-win-win, despite opening the sluice for <3% of the study period, given safe downstream passage was maximised, the financial benefits of sluicing water (∼£14,670 in direct operational costs over two years) and the relative ease of implementation.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Carter, Liam J.","Wright, Rosalind M.","Thomas, Robert E.","Reeds, Jake","Murphy, Leona A.","Collier, Stephen J.","Evans, Oliver","Baktoft, Henrik","Bolland, Jonathan D."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-694875"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bolland, Jonathan D."],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Environment Agency","University of Hull"],"keyword":["Anguilla","European eel","Fish passage","Migration","Pumping station"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"timing is everything operational changes at a pumping station with a gravity sluice to provide safe downstream passage for silver european eels and deliver considerable financial savings","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jenvman.2023.119143","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-694875","identifier":[{"id":"85173156741","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37804626","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-45f2e741-60f0-450a-870b-c98f8edea376"],"keyword":["Anguilla","European eel","Fish passage","Gravity sluice","Migration","Pumping station"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B0BA8DE5A818CC7F2A940E930631522E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jenvman.2023.119143","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/371243745/1-s2.0-S030147972301931X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of hull","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hull","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"environment agency","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Environment Agency","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Freshwater Fisheries Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liam J.","key":"carterpau","last":"Carter","name":"Carter, Liam J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosalind M.","key":"wrightpau","last":"Wright","name":"Wright, Rosalind M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert E.","key":"thomaspau","last":"Thomas","name":"Thomas, Robert E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jake","key":"reedspau","last":"Reeds","name":"Reeds, Jake","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leona A.","key":"murphypau","last":"Murphy","name":"Murphy, Leona A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephen J.","key":"collierpau","last":"Collier","name":"Collier, Stephen J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver","key":"evanspau","last":"Evans","name":"Evans, Oliver","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"baktoftpau","last":"Baktoft","locid":"642a7cea-4ecc-4866-97f3-0d86f3e47ec0","name":"Baktoft, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-3644-4960","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan D.","key":"bollandpau","last":"Bolland","name":"Bolland, Jonathan D.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37804626"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jenvman.2023.119143","issn":["03014797","10958630"],"issn_org":["03014797"],"journal":"Journal of Environmental Management","paperid":"119143","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Environmental Management","volume":"347"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173156741"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-45f2e741-60f0-450a-870b-c98f8edea376"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Timing is everything; operational changes at a pumping station with a gravity sluice to provide safe downstream passage for silver European eels and deliver considerable financial savings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-694875","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Twenty-six years ago a small committee report, building on earlier studies, expounded a compelling and poetic vision for the future of astronomy, calling for an infrared-optimized space telescope with an aperture of at least 4 m. With the support of their governments in the US, Europe, and Canada, 20,000 people realized that vision as the 6.5 m James Webb Space Telescope. A generation of astronomers will celebrate their accomplishments for the life of the mission, potentially as long as 20 yr, and beyond. This report and the scientific discoveries that follow are extended thank-you notes to the 20,000 team members. The telescope is working perfectly, with much better image quality than expected. In this and accompanying papers, we give a brief history, describe the observatory, outline its objectives and current observing program, and discuss the inventions and people who made it possible. We cite detailed reports on the design and the measured performance on orbit.","author_count":1039,"contributors":["Gardner, Jonathan P.","Mather, John C.","Abbott, Randy","Abell, James S.","Abernathy, Mark","Abney, Faith E.","Abraham, John G.","Abraham, Roberto","Abul-Huda, Yasin M.","Acton, Scott","Adams, Cynthia K.","Adams, Evan","Adler, David S.","Adriaensen, Maarten","Aguilar, Jonathan Albert","Ahmed, Mansoor","Ahmed, Nasif S.","Ahmed, Tanjira","Albat, Rüdeger","Albert, Loïc","Alberts, Stacey","Aldridge, David","Allen, Mary Marsha","Allen, Shaune S.","Altenburg, Martin","Altunc, Serhat","Alvarez, Jose Lorenzo","Álvarez-Márquez, Javier","Oliveira, Catarina Alves de","Ambrose, Leslie L.","Anandakrishnan, Satya M.","Andersen, Gregory C.","Anderson, Harry James","Anderson, Jay","Anderson, Kristen","Anderson, Sara M.","Aprea, Julio","Archer, Benita J.","Arenberg, Jonathan W.","Argyriou, Ioannis","Arribas, Santiago","Artigau, Étienne","Arvai, Amanda Rose","Atcheson, Paul","Atkinson, Charles B.","Averbukh, Jesse","Aymergen, Cagatay","Bacinski, John J.","Baggett, Wayne E