{"abstract":"Domestic cats were derived from the Near Eastern wildcat (Felis lybica), after which they dispersed with people into Europe. As they did so, it is possible that they interbred with the indigenous population of European wildcats (Felis silvestris). Gene flow between incoming domestic animals and closely related indigenous wild species has been previously demonstrated in other taxa, including pigs, sheep, goats, bees, chickens, and cattle. In the case of cats, a lack of nuclear, genome-wide data, particularly from Near Eastern wildcats, has made it difficult to either detect or quantify this possibility. To address these issues, we generated 75 ancient mitochondrial genomes, 14 ancient nuclear genomes, and 31 modern nuclear genomes from European and Near Eastern wildcats. Our results demonstrate that despite cohabitating for at least 2,000 years on the European mainland and in Britain, most modern domestic cats possessed less than 10% of their ancestry from European wildcats, and ancient European wildcats possessed little to no ancestry from domestic cats. The antiquity and strength of this reproductive isolation between introduced domestic cats and local wildcats was likely the result of behavioral and ecological differences. Intriguingly, this long-lasting reproductive isolation is currently being eroded in parts of the species’ distribution as a result of anthropogenic activities.","author_count":57,"contributors":["Jamieson, Alexandra","Carmagnini, Alberto","Howard-McCombe, Jo","Doherty, Sean","Hirons, Alexandra","Dimopoulos, Evangelos","Lin, Audrey T.","Allen, Richard","Anderson-Whymark, Hugo","Barnett, Ross","Batey, Colleen","Beglane, Fiona","Bowden, Will","Bratten, John","De Cupere, Bea","Drew, Ellie","Foley, Nicole M.","Fowler, Tom","Fox, Allison","Geigl, Eva-Maria","Gotfredsen, Anne Birgitte","Grange, Thierry","Griffiths, David","Groß, Daniel","Haruda, Ashleigh","Hjermind, Jesper","Knapp, Zoe","Lebrasseur, Ophélie","Librado, Pablo","Lyons, Leslie A.","Mainland, Ingrid","McDonnell, Christine","Muñoz-Fuentes, Violeta","Nowak, Carsten","O'Connor, Terry","Peters, Joris","Russo, Isa-Rita M.","Ryan, Hannah","Sheridan, Alison","Sinding, Mikkel Holger S.","Skoglund, Pontus","Swali, Pooja","Symmons, Robert","Thomas, Gabor","Jensen, Theis Zetner Trolle","Kitchener, Andrew C.","Senn, Helen","Lawson, Daniel","Driscoll, Carlos","Murphy, William J.","Beaumont, Mark","Ottoni, Claudio","Sykes, Naomi","Larson, Greger","Frantz, Laurent"],"cuid":["S02-099.04-704554"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","France","Germany","Ireland","Italy","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Atlantic Technological University","Bavarian Natural History Collections","Cardiff University","Department of Anthropology, National Museum of Natural History, Smithsonian Institution, Washington D.C","Department of Archaeology, University of Exeter, Exeter, Devon, UK","Durham University","European Molecular Biology Laboratory","Fishbourne Roman Palace","Forschungsinstitut Senckenberg","Galton Corp. (Biz)","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität","National Museums of Scotland","Paris-Cité University","Queen Mary University of London","RZSS WildGenes Laboratory, Royal Zoological Society of Scotland","Royal Belgian Institute of Natural Sciences","Royal Zoological Society of Scotland","School of Biological and Chemical Science, Queen Mary University of London, London, U.K.","Smithsonian Institution","Texas A&M University","The Francis Crick Institute","University West of Florida","University of Bristol","University of Cambridge","University of Edinburgh","University of Exeter","University of Missouri","University of Nottingham","University of Oxford","University of Reading","University of Rome Tor Vergata","University of York","University of the Highlands and Islands","Université Paul Sabatier Toulouse III","York Archaeological Trust"],"keyword":["Ancient DNA","Cats","Domestication","Hybridization","Palaeogenomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"],"OT":["Manx Museum"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"limited historical admixture between european wildcats and domestic cats","src":["ku","kum"],"src-code":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2023.08.031","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.04-704554","identifier":[{"id":"37935117","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85175537698","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0663df40-0c96-43a5-8e0b-6db1cbccc79e","kum-43a2ea09-1e9d-4a68-8565-c4aec9756964"],"keyword":["Palaeogenomics","ancient DNA","cats","domestication","hybridization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E4A50D3AAF092524696B80E1CF9ACD2C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2023.08.031","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/372811627/1_s2.0_S0960982223010734_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilians universität","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität","u