},{"affno":"10","country":"us","key":"university of pittsburgh","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Pittsburgh","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"jp","key":"asahikawa medical university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Asahikawa Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"12","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"fuchsbuderpau","last":"Fuchs-Buder","name":"Fuchs-Buder, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sorin J.","key":"brullpau","last":"Brull","name":"Brull, Sorin J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Malin Jonsson","key":"fagerlundpau","last":"Fagerlund","name":"Fagerlund, Malin Jonsson","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"J. Ross","key":"renewpau","last":"Renew","name":"Renew, J. Ross","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Guy","key":"cammupau","last":"Cammu","name":"Cammu, Guy","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Glenn S.","key":"murphypau","last":"Murphy","name":"Murphy, Glenn S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Michiel","key":"warlépau","last":"Warlé","name":"Warlé, Michiel","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Matias","key":"vestedpau","last":"Vested","locid":"b39be0f7-6164-46e6-bb9f-0025b298dbbe","name":"Vested, Matias","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Béla","key":"fülesdipau","last":"Fülesdi","name":"Fülesdi, Béla","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Reka","key":"nemespau","last":"Nemes","name":"Nemes, Reka","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Malachy O.","key":"columbpau","last":"Columb","name":"Columb, Malachy O.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Daniela","key":"damianpau","last":"Damian","name":"Damian, Daniela","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Peter J.","key":"davispau","last":"Davis","name":"Davis, Peter J.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","first":"Hajime","key":"iwasakipau","last":"Iwasaki","name":"Iwasaki, Hajime","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","first":"Lars I.","key":"erikssonpau","last":"Eriksson","name":"Eriksson, Lars I.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37345870"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14279","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"8","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"994-1017","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85162693630"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d14fcb72-4725-4e82-93c9-e5f6bec16509"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Good clinical research practice (GCRP) in pharmacodynamic studies of neuromuscular blocking agents III : The 2023 Geneva revision","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-749194","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"No previous study has examined the large-scale distributional drivers of the entire global pool of 3,499 macrophyte species, despite the obvious importance of this for understanding the macroecology of these plants. To assess the hypothesis that natural rather than human-related transfer vectors act as the primary long-distance drivers of global movement of aquatic macrophytes, we analysed current macrophyte species distributions in relation to a set of human-related and natural transfer vectors. Most macrophytes (2,492 species: 71.2% of the global total) are endemic to a single ecozone, and generally lack the various functional adaptations needed for successful long-distance propagule transport. Such traits are, however, common in the 1,007 (28.8%) species native in > 1 ecozone. In total, 779 species (22.3%) are introduced, naturalised or invasive (I species) in one or more ecozones outwith their native range. The proportion of I species varies between ecozones and is best predicted by annual temperature and longitude. A migratory bird transfer vector and climatic variables strongly predict global native macrophyte species occurrence. Some native species of Miocene origin (or older) may have had their world distribution influenced by ancient vicariance events, while inter-ecozone hydrochory and Late Quaternary climate change are also relevant factors influencing a few species.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Lobato-de Magalhães, Tatiana","Murphy, Kevin","Efremov, Andrey","Davidson, Thomas Alexander","Molina-Navarro, Eugenio","Wood, Kevin A.","Tapia-Grimaldo, Julissa","Hofstra, Deborah","Fu, Hui","Ortegón-Aznar, Ileana"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-243525"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["China","Mexico","New Zealand","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hunan Agricultural University","NIWA","Universidad Autonoma Queretaro","Universidad Autonoma de Yucatan","University of Alcalá","University of Glasgow","Wildfowl and Wetlands Trust"],"keyword":["Invasiveness","Long distance movement","Plant distribution","Zoochory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how on earth did that get there natural and human vectors of aquatic macrophyte global distribution","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85143810287","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-243525","identifier":[{"id":"85143810287","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c7f346df-f60f-4822-b183-e998cfbecc3f"],"keyword":["Ancient vicariance","Anthropochory","Invasiveness","Long-distance movement","Plant distribution","Zoochory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A05BF232C6BC7E206A04037B15CF407"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"mx","key":"universidad autonoma queretaro","loc":["Mexico","America, Central","OECD"],"name":"Universidad Autonoma Queretaro","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of glasgow","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Glasgow","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Freshwater Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"es","key":"university of alcalá","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Alcalá","used":1},{"affno":"5","cou