105132","issn":["03063674","14730480"],"issn_org":["03063674"],"issue":"20","journal":"British Journal of Sports Medicine","pages":"1157-1170","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Sports Medicine","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137660444"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bf9bc8f5-58ab-499e-8f02-a17d4250f6e3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Physical activity, sedentary time and breast cancer risk : a Mendelian randomisation study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-507772","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Individuals who demonstrate well-founded fears of persecution or face real risk of being subjected to torture, are eligible for asylum under Danish law. Decision outcomes, however, are often influenced by the subjective perceptions of the asylum applicant's credibility. Literature reports on correlations between asylum outcomes and various extra-legal factors. Artificial Intelligence has often been used to uncover such correlations and highlight the predictability of the asylum outcomes. In this work, we employ a dataset of asylum decisions in Denmark to study the variations in recognition rates, on the basis of several application features, such as the applicant's nationality, identified gender, religion etc. We use Machine Learning classifiers to assess the predictability of the cases' outcomes on the basis of such features. We find that depending on the classifier, and the considered features, different predictability outcomes arise. We highlight, therefore, the need to take such discrepancies into account, before drawing conclusions with regards to the causes of the outcomes' predictability.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Katsikouli, Panagiota","Byrne, William Hamilton","Gammeltoft-Hansen, Thomas","Høgenhaug, Anna Murphy","Møller, Naja Holten","Nielsen, Trine Rask","Olsen, Henrik Palmer","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695701"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automated decision making","Machine learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"machine learning and asylum adjudications from analysis of variations to outcome predictions","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2022.3229053","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695701","identifier":[{"id":"85144776075","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3fc39823-925c-4176-b2a2-16f5845add1d"],"keyword":["Asylum adjudications","automated decision-making","machine learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7FD172D09265F96C1460974AA8D5927F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2022.3229053","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Law, Area of Research, Centre of Excellence for International Courts and Governance","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Panagiota","key":"katsikoulipau","last":"Katsikouli","locid":"226083e7-02c8-46e2-950c-c199c09877e4","name":"Katsikouli, Panagiota","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"William H.","key":"byrnepau","last":"Byrne","locid":"930d34e1-4a5f-4111-9a05-5b5b35c6f6b0","name":"Byrne, William Hamilton","name_org":"Byrne, William H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"gammeltofthansenpau","last":"Gammeltoft-Hansen","locid":"782edd72-af25-4d5f-9795-455619228ae9","name":"Gammeltoft-Hansen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-1518-137X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Hojberg","key":"hogenhaugpau","last":"Hogenhaug","locid":"c13954df-c43d-4588-adf6-3d36914b3abb","name":"Høgenhaug, Anna Murphy","name_org":"Hogenhaug, Anna Hojberg","orcid":"0009-0004-6715-0561","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Naja Holten","key":"mollerpau","last":"Moller","locid":"1373f0c3-8420-4023-874a-25270bf667d6","name":"Møller, Naja Holten","name_org":"Moller, Naja Holten","orcid":"0000-0002-4324-3745","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Trine Rask","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ac2c38a7-b5dd-47eb-b3ff-37af0e55305a","name":"Nielsen, Trine Rask","orcid":"0000-0002-9787-9052","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Palmer","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d6151186-5867-4059-bc35-8e82ae4be33e","name":"Olsen, Henrik Palmer","orcid":"0000-0001-8486-8752","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/access.2022.3229053","issn":["21693536"],"journal":"IEEE Access","pages":"130955-130967","status":"p","title":"IEEE Access","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144776075"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3fc39823-925c-4176-b2a2-16f5845add1d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Machine Learning and Asylum Adjudications : From Analysis of Variations to Outcome Predictions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695701","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Multiplanet systems are valuable arenas for investigating exoplanet architectures and comparing planetary siblings. TOI-1246 is one such system, with a moderately bright K dwarf (V = 11.6, K = 9.9) and four transiting sub-Neptunes identified by TESS with orbital periods of 4.31, 5.90, 18.66, and 37.92 days. We collected 130 radial velocity observations with Keck/HIRES and TNG/HARPS-N to measure planet masses. We refit the 14 sectors of TESS photometry to refine planet radii (2.97 +/- 0.06 R (circle plus), 2.47 +/- 0.08 R (circle plus), 3.46 +/- 0.09 R (circle plus), and 3.72 +/- 0.16 R (circle plus)) and confirm the four planets. We find that TOI-1246 e is substantially more massive than the three inner planets (8.1 +/- 1.1 M (circle plus), 8.8 +/- 1.2 M (circle plus), 5.3 +/- 1.7 M (circle plus), and 14.8 +/- 2.3 M (circle plus)). The two outer planets, TOI-1246 d and TOI-1246 e, lie near to the 2:1 resonance (P (e)/P ( d ) = 2.03) and exhibit transit-timing variations. TOI-1246 is one of the brightest four-planet systems, making it amenable for continued observations. It is one of only five systems with measured masses and radii for all four transiting planets. The planet densities range from 0.70 +/- 0.24 to 3.21 +/- 0.44 g cm(-3), implying a range of bulk and atmospheric compositions. We also report a fifth planet candidate found in the RV data with a minimum mass of 25.6 +/- 3.6 M (circle plus). This planet candidate is exterior to TOI-1246 e, with a candidate period of 93.8 days, and we discuss the implications if it is confirmed to be planetary in nature.","author_count":81,"contributors":["Turtelboom, Emma","Weiss, Lauren M.","Dressing, Courtney D.","Nowak, Grzegorz","Palle, Enric","Beard, Corey","Blunt, Sarah","Brinkman, Casey","Chontos, Ashley","Claytor, Zachary R.","Dai, Fei","Dalba, Paul A.","Giacalone, Steven","Gonzales, Erica","Harada, Caleb K.","Hill, Michelle L.","Holcomb, Rae","Korth, Judith","Lubin, Jack","Masseron, Thomas","MacDougall