ecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"I.","key":"zychoripau","last":"Zychor","name":"Zychor, I.","rank":1251,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1741-4326/ab2276","issn":["00295515","10185577"],"issn_org":["00295515"],"issue":"11","journal":"Nuclear Fusion","paperid":"112021","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Nuclear Fusion","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070875113"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-412de8ed-b09a-46d9-b4bf-aa62f2373904"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Overview of the JET preparation for deuterium-tritium operation with the ITER like-wall","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-323976","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Human corneal transplantation (keratoplasty) is typically considered to have superior short- and long-term outcomes and lower requirement for immunosuppression compared to solid organ transplants because of the inherent immune privilege and tolerogenic mechanisms associated with the anterior segment of the eye. However, in a substantial proportion of corneal transplants, the rates of acute rejection and/or graft failure are comparable to or greater than those of the commonly transplanted solid organs. Critically, while registry data and observational studies have helped to identify factors that are associated with increased risk of corneal transplant failure, the extent to which these risk factors operate through enhancing immune-mediated rejection is less clear. In this overview, we summarize a range of important recent clinical and basic insights related to high-risk corneal transplantation, the factors associated with graft failure, and the immunological basis of corneal allograft rejection. We highlight critical research areas from which continued progress is likely to drive improvements in the long-term survival of high-risk corneal transplants. These include further development and clinical testing of predictive risk scores and assays; greater use of multicenter clinical trials to optimize immunosuppressive therapy in high-risk recipients and robust clinical translation of novel, mechanistically-targeted immunomodulatory and regenerative therapies that are emerging from basic science laboratories. We also emphasize the relative lack of knowledge regarding transplant outcomes for infection-related corneal diseases that are common in the developing world and the potential for greater cross-pollination and synergy between corneal and solid organ transplant research communities.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Armitage, W John","Goodchild, Christine","Griffin, Matthew D","Gunn, David J","Hjortdal, Jesper","Lohan, Paul","Murphy, Conor C","Pleyer, Uwe","Ritter, Thomas","Tole, Derek M","Vabres, Bertrand"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-142588"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","Ireland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CHU Nantes","Charité-Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Royal College of Surgeons in Ireland","University Hospitals Bristol and Weston NHS Foundation Trust","University of Bristol"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high risk corneal transplantation recent developments and future possibilities","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/TP.0000000000002938","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-142588","identifier":[{"id":"85075510819","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31765363","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6867666","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-16ecc5ad-1b5b-4288-a29e-9ffa7ebb3c11"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9BA33563D59BE06857068A18D90A0461"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/TP.0000000000002938","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/196447671/tp_103_2468.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of bristol","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bristol","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ie","key":"royal college of surgeons in ireland","loc":["I