{"abstract":"Cl- channel protein 1 (ClC-1) may be important for excitability and contractility in skeletal muscle, but ClC-1 abundance has not been examined in human muscle. The aim of the present study was to examine ClC-1 abundance in human skeletal muscle, including fibre type specific differences and the effect of exercise training. A commercially available antibody was tested with positive and negative control tissue, and it recognised specifically ClC-1 in the range from 100-150 kDa. Abundance of ClC-1 was 38% higher (P < 0.01) in fast twitch Type IIa muscle fibres than in slow twitch Type I. Muscle ClC-1 abundance did not change with four weeks of training consisting of 30 min cycling at 85% of maximal heart rate (HRmax) and 3×30-s all out sprints or during a 7-week training period with 10-12×30 s uphill cycling and 4-5×~4 min cycling at 90-95% of HRmax. ClC-1 abundance correlated negatively (P < 0.01) with maximal oxygen consumption (r = -0.552) and incremental exercise performance (r = -0.546). In addition, trained cyclists had lower (P < 0.01) ClC-1 abundance than lesser trained individuals. The present observations indicate that a low abundance of muscle ClC-1 may be beneficial for exercise performance, but the role of abundance and regulation of ClC-1 in skeletal muscle of humans with respect to exercise performance and trainability need to be elucidated.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Thomassen, Martin","Hostrup, Morten","Murphy, Robyn M","Cromer, Brett A","Skovgaard, Casper","Gunnarsson, Thomas Gunnar Petursson","Christensen, Peter Møller","Bangsbo, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-411525"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","La Trobe University"],"keyword":["ADR","Antibody Specificity","Excitability","Faculty of Science","Performance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Department of Chemistry and Biotechnology, Swinburne University."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"abundance of clc 000000000001 chloride channel in human skeletal muscle fibre type specific differences and effect of training","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-411525","identifier":[{"id":"85058990159","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29722626","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1e6565d0-1639-4868-bc8e-60f31962d189"],"keyword":["ADR","Antibody specificity","Arrested development of righting response","Excitability","Faculty of Science","Performance","Proteine expression","Single fiber","Single fibre"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-567184F5F8E55FC1C4DC8D46BF59F7F2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Human Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"la trobe university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"La Trobe University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Chemistry and Biotechnology, Swinburne University."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"thomassenpau","last":"Thomassen","locid":"20bc3fb3-0877-4809-b3bf-0c7eed381b89","name":"Thomassen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-7503-6815","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"hostruppau","last":"Hostrup","locid":"2c96b73f-d427-45db-af64-9caf29101092","name":"Hostrup, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-6201-2483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Robyn M","key":"murphypau","last":"Murphy","name":"Murphy, Robyn M","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Brett A","key":"cromerpau","last":"Cromer","name":"Cromer, Brett A","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Casper","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"7611187e-c4a8-4c64-806c-2a62b4d9136e","name":"Skovgaard, Casper","orcid":"0000-0001-5778-9581","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Petursson","key":"gunnarssonpau","last":"Gunnarsson","locid":"e3c6dd6c-732a-4289-9027-41a5112a99d9","name":"Gunnarsson, Thomas Gunnar Petursson","name_org":"Gunnarsson, Thomas Petursson","orcid":"0000-0001-7414-3045","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Møller","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"e3f1d227-5890-4e68-b753-fcd26ec7c068","name":"Christensen, Peter Møller","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"bangsbopau","last":"Bangsbo","locid":"24839560-f889-42a6-9b73-97b69f101548","name":"Bangsbo, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-1305-9274","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29722626"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/japplphysiol.01042.2017","issn":["15221601","87507587"],"issn_org":["87507587"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Applied Physiology","pages":"470-478","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Physiology","volume":"125"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058990159"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1e6565d0-1639-4868-bc8e-60f31962d189"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Abundance of ClC-1 chloride channel in human skeletal muscle : Fibre type specific differences and effect of training","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-411525","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Disorders of the brain can exhibit considerable epidemiological comorbidity and often share symptoms, provoking debate about their etiologic overlap. We quantified the genetic sharing of 25 brain disorders from genome-wide association studies of 265,218 patients and 784,643 control participants and assessed their relationship to 17 phenotypes from 1,191,588 individuals. Psychiatric disorders share common variant risk, whereas neurological disorders appear more distinct from one another and from the psychiatric disorders. We also identified significant sharing between disorders and a number of brain phenotypes, including cognitive measures. Further, we conducted simulations to explore how statistical power, diagnostic misclassification, and phenotypic heterogeneity affect genetic correlations. These results highlight the importance of common genetic variation as a risk factor for brain disorders and the value of heritability-based methods in understanding their etiology.","author_count":577,"contributors":["Anttila, Verneri","Bulik-Sullivan, Brendan","Finucane, Hilary K.","Walters, Raymond K.","Bras, Jose","Duncan, Laramie","Escott-Price, Valentina","Falcone, Guido J.","Gormley, Padhraig","Malik, Rainer","Patsopoulos, Nikolaos A.","Ripke, Stephan","Wei, Zhi","Yu, Dongmei","Lee, Phil H.","Turley, Patrick","Grenier-Boley, Benjamin","Chouraki, Vincent","Kamatani, Yoichiro","Berr, Claudine","Letenneur, Luc","Hannequin, Didier","Amouyel, Philippe","Boland, Anne","Deleuze, Jean-François","Duron, Emmanuelle","Vardarajan, Badri N.","Reitz, Christiane","Goate, Alison M.","Huentelman, Matthew J.","Kamboh, M. Ilyas","Larson, Eric B.","Rogaeva, Ekaterina","St George-Hyslop, Peter","Hakonarson, Hakon","Kukull, Walter A.","Farrer, Lindsay A.","Barnes, Lisa L.","Beach, Thomas G.","Demirci, F. Yesim","Head, Elizabeth","Hulette, Christine M.","Jicha, Gregory A.","Kauwe, John S.k.","Kaye, Jeffrey A.","Leverenz, James B.","Levey, Allan I.","Lieberman, Andrew P.","Pankratz,