{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Genomic studies of endangered species provide insights into their evolution and demographic history, reveal patterns of genomic erosion that might limit their viability, and offer tools for their effective conservation. The Iberian lynx (Lynx pardinus) is the most endangered felid and a unique example of a species on the brink of extinction. RESULTS: We generate the first annotated draft of the Iberian lynx genome and carry out genome-based analyses of lynx demography, evolution, and population genetics. We identify a series of severe population bottlenecks in the history of the Iberian lynx that predate its known demographic decline during the 20th century and have greatly impacted its genome evolution. We observe drastically reduced rates of weak-to-strong substitutions associated with GC-biased gene conversion and increased rates of fixation of transposable elements. We also find multiple signatures of genetic erosion in the two remnant Iberian lynx populations, including a high frequency of potentially deleterious variants and substitutions, as well as the lowest genome-wide genetic diversity reported so far in any species. CONCLUSIONS: The genomic features observed in the Iberian lynx genome may hamper short- and long-term viability through reduced fitness and adaptive potential. The knowledge and resources developed in this study will boost the research on felid evolution and conservation genomics and will benefit the ongoing conservation and management of this emblematic species.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Abascal, Federico","Corvelo, André","Cruz, Fernando","Villanueva-Cañas, José L","Vlasova, Anna","Marcet-Houben, Marina","Martínez-Cruz, Begoña","Cheng, Jade Yu","Prieto, Pablo","Quesada, Víctor","Quilez, Javier","Li, Gang","García, Francisca","Rubio-Camarillo, Miriam","Frias, Leonor","Ribeca, Paolo","Capella-Gutiérrez, Salvador","Rodríguez, José M","Câmara, Francisco","Lowy, Ernesto","Cozzuto, Luca","Erb, Ionas","Tress, Michael L","Rodriguez-Ales, Jose L","Ruiz-Orera, Jorge","Reverter, Ferran","Casas-Marce, Mireia","Soriano, Laura","Arango, Javier R","Derdak, Sophia","Galán, Beatriz","Blanc, Julie","Gut, Marta","Lorente-Galdos, Belen","Andrés-Nieto, Marta","López-Otín, Carlos","Valencia, Alfonso","Gut, Ivo","García, José L","Guigó, Roderic","Murphy, William J","Ruiz-Herrera, Aurora","Marques-Bonet, Tomas","Roma, Guglielmo","Notredame, Cedric","Mailund, Thomas","Albà, M Mar","Gabaldón, Toni","Alioto, Tyler","Godoy, José A"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-190677"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Autonomous University of Barcelona","Centro Nacional de Analisis Genomico (CNAG)","Centro Nacional de Investigaciones Oncológicas (CNIO)","Consejo Superior de Investigaciones Científicas (CSIC)","Municipal Institute for Medical Research Hospital del Mar","Pompeu Fabra University","Texas A and M University","University of Oviedo"],"keyword":["Conservation genomics","Genetic diversity","Genetic drift","Inbreeding","Lynx"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extreme genomic erosion after recurrent demographic bottlenecks in the highly endangered iberian lynx","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85004009724","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-190677","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5155386","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85004009724","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27964752","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6b832109-450e-4cf9-9e67-275dc67c9cc1"],"keyword":["Conservation genomics","Genetic diversity","Genetic drift","Inbreeding","Lynx"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-993BD757CCA7336BD0FA5D30E113034E"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"es","key":"centro nacional de investigaciones oncológicas","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Centro Nacional de Investigaciones Oncológicas (CNIO)","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"centro nacional de analisis genomico","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Centro Nacional de Analisis Genomico (CNAG)","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"es","key":"municipal institute for medical research hospital del mar","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Municipal Institute for Medical Research Hospital del Mar","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"es","key":"consejo superior de investigaciones científicas","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Consejo Superior de Investigaciones Científicas (CSIC)","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Bioinformatics Research Centre (BiRC)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"es","key":"university of oviedo","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oviedo","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"es","key":"pompeu fabra university","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Pompeu Fabra Universi