{"abstract":"This paper presents the first major data release and survey description for the ANUWiFeS SuperNovA Programme. ANU WiFeS SuperNovA Programme is an ongoing supernova spectroscopy campaign utilising the Wide Field Spectrograph on the Australian National University 2.3-m telescope. The first and primary data release of this programme (AWSNAP-DR1) releases 357 spectra of 175 unique objects collected over 82 equivalent full nights of observing from 2012 July to 2015 August. These spectra have been made publicly available via the WISEREP supernova spectroscopy repository. We analyse the ANUWiFeS SuperNovA Programme sample of Type Ia supernova spectra, including measurements of narrow sodium absorption features afforded by the high spectral resolution of the Wide Field Spectrograph instrument. In some cases, we were able to use the integral-field nature of the Wide Field Spectrograph instrument to measure the rotation velocity of the SN host galaxy near the SN location in order to obtain precision sodium absorption velocities. We also present an extensive time series of SN 2012dn, including a near-nebular spectrum which both confirms its 'super-Chandrasekhar' status and enables measurement of the sub-solar host metallicity at the SN site.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Childress, Michael J.","Tucker, Brad E.","Yuan, Fang","Scalzo, Richard","Ruiter, Ashley","Seitenzahl, Ivo","Zhang, Bonnie","Schmidt, Brian","Anguiano, Borja","Aniyan, Suryashree","Bayliss, Daniel D. R.","Bento, Joao","Bessell, Michael","Bian, Fuyan","Davies, Rebecca","Dopita, Michael","Fogarty, Lisa","Fraser-McKelvie, Amelia","Freeman, Ken","Kuruwita, Rajika","Medling, Anne M.","Murphy, Simon J.","Murphy, Simon J.","Owers, Matthew","Panther, Fiona","Sweet, Sarah M.","Thomas, Adam D.","Zhou, George"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-177315"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Childress, Michael J."],"country":["Australia","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Australian National University","Harvard University","Macquarie University","Monash University","University of Geneva","University of Southampton","University of Sydney"],"keyword":["Core collapse supernovae","Digital sky survey","FIELD SPECTROGRAPH WIFES","HIGH VELOCITY FEATURES","IA SUPERNOVAE","MASS METALLICITY RELATION","Optical spectra","SN 2011FE","Star forming galaxies","Supernovae general","white dwarf"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the anu wifes supernova programme awsnap","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1607.08526.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-177315","identifier":[{"id":"000388186700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"84994576010","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-54209d0c-119a-49cb-b80e-f3bbfe33a8ed"],"keyword":["CORE-COLLAPSE SUPERNOVAE","DIGITAL SKY SURVEY","FIELD SPECTROGRAPH WIFES","HIGH-VELOCITY FEATURES","IA SUPERNOVAE","MASS-METALLICITY RELATION","OPTICAL-SPECTRA","SN 2011FE","STAR-FORMING GALAXIES","WHITE-DWARF","supernovae: general","supernovae: individual: (SN 2012dn)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4C86482BAC4689969810971BDD5A635B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1607.08526.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of southampton","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of 